  🤐 Which answers a layer compresses, and the layer:

    🧱 app 🤐 app 🆕🤐❗️❗️❗️

  An answer is compressed, as gzip, for a client whose Accept-Encoding takes
  gzip, when it has a body in memory of 1,024 bytes to a megabyte; a type
  that is text (text of any kind, JSON, XML, JavaScript, SVG, or one the
  options were told of); a status other than 204, 206 and 304; no
  Content-Encoding and no Content-Range; no Cache-Control that says
  no-transform; and when the stream is smaller than the body. A body that is
  written while it is sent, as a file's is, is left as it is.

  Every answer that could have been compressed says Vary: Accept-Encoding,
  compressed or not, so that a cache does not hand one client the bytes of
  another. A strong ETag becomes a weak one on a compressed answer, whose
  bytes are others. Every setter returns the options.
